      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under vacuum using Schlenk techniques, a solution of PhOK (0.52 g, 3.93 mmol) in THF (15 mL) was added at room temperature to a suspension of NdI2H (0.80 g, 2.00 mmol) in THF (5 mL). Gas evolution and dissolution of black NdI2H were observed. The mixture was stirred for 5 h in a sealed ampoule. The blue-violet solution was decanted from a colorless powder-like precipitate and the solvent was removed by slow evaporation. The deposited blue-violet fine-crystalline powder was washed with cold THF and dried in vacuum. Crystals for X-ray analysis were obtained by slow concentration of a THF/hexane solution.",
